From 5bf25324ea608e910a16fde8f36d2d9be7f40696 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sbkz34 <sbkz34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:29:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run on Mali GPUs without vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics

Mali drivers (e.g. Mali-G720 on Dimensity 9400-class chips) do not expose
vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics, so the SDK refused the device and the game
never started.

The SDK already has the fallbacks: the SPIR-V translator leaves memory
export out of vertex shaders when the feature is missing and marks the
shared memory NonWritable. Only the hard checks stood in the way.

- patch 0038: vulkan_require_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics (until now
  "deprecated and ignored") is honoured again, default false. Without the
  feature the device is accepted, and vertex-shader memexport draws run
  without the export instead of being dropped. vulkan_mask_features also
  accepts vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics, so the path can be tried on
  Adreno.
- launcher passes --vulkan_require_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics=false
  next to the existing Mali flags.
- Vulkan probe and custom driver check no longer treat the feature as
  required; the probe notes that vertex memexport is skipped.

GPUs that have the feature are unaffected.

